<title>GREECE: IFC sets terms on two Marathon FRN issues.</title>
<headline>IFC sets terms on two Marathon FRN issues.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following information on two drachma FRNs issued by the IFC was provided by joint lead managers Barclays Bank PLC, Athens branch and the National Bank of Greece.</p>
<p> ISSUER	     IFC		   ISSUE AMOUNT 12.1 BLN DRACH</p>
<p> ISSUE DATE	 EXPECTED NOV 96   TYPE  FRN</p>
<p> ISSUE PRICE	TO BE DETERMINED</p>
<p> PAYMENT DATE     DEC 31, 96	  MATURITY  APRIL 30, 99</p>
<p> INTEREST RATE			    6-MTH ATHIBOR LESS 50 BPS</p>
<p> INTEREST RATE/FIRST PERIOD	   3-MTH ATHIBOR LESS 50 BPS</p>
<p> INTEREST PAYMENT		  SEMI-ANNUAL, APRIl 30 AND OCT 31,</p>
<p>					 FIRST SHORT COUPON APRIL 30, 97</p>
<p> LISTING	    ATHENS STOCK EXCHANGE</p>
<p> ISSUER		 IFC		 ISSUE AMOUNT  14.6 BLN DRACH</p>
<p> TYPE		   FRN WITH ONE TIME CAPITAL REDEMPTION</p>
<p> ISSUE DATE	   EXPECTED NOV 96</p>
<p> ISSUE PRICE	  TO BE DETERMINED</p>
<p> PAYMENT DATE	 DEC 31, 96	  MATURITY  DEC 31, 2000</p>
<p> CAPITAL REDEMPTION DATE		  DEC 31, 98</p>
<p> AMOUNT OF CAPITAL REDEEMED	     5.4 BLN DRACH</p>
<p> MATURITY DATE	DEC 31, 2000</p>
<p> FACE VALUE AT MATURITY		   9.2 BLN DRACH</p>
<p> INTEREST   RATE			    6-MTH ATHIBOR LESS 50BPS</p>
<p> INTEREST PAYMENT   SEMI-ANNUAL	 JUN 30 AND DEC 31</p>
<p> LISTING		ATHENS STOCK EXCHANGE</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
